  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[node_content]` is a fenced commentary citation on an explicit function with a body. That is a permitted form.\n\n- **Substantive reason:** `node_content` is a deliberate guard. It only panics with \"storage operations must not read graph contents\". The commentary says the `Domain` trait requires the callback, but this storage-only fixture must never resolve contents. It also says other fixtures exercise content resolution. The source supports this.\n- **Agrees with the source:** `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` only delegate to `FileEvidenceStorage` using `node_path`. `NodeContent` is the uninhabited `UnreadContents`, so no content value can exist. A test that reached the guard would fail on purpose, so zero execution is the expected outcome.\n- **Callers:** The only users of `StoredGraph` are tests in `tests/storage.rs`. The `execute` of `StoredReview` reads no nodes. `dependencies_are_current` and `prepare_read` call `node_content` only for node dependencies or reads, and this fixture's criterion makes none. The no-read premise is therefore consistent with the callers I reviewed.\n- **Other rules:** The item has no `{impl}` or `{test}` reference to `habeas:coverage`, so the citation is not redundant. Nothing in the item needs a different role.",
